    "lp_how_it_works": {
      "type": "lp-media-text",
      "name": "LP · Media + text",
      "blocks": {
        "p1": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "lead": "Insulin sensitivity.",
            "text": "Supports how well your cells respond to insulin and steadier blood sugar.†"
          }
        },
        "p2": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "lead": "Ovulation.",
            "text": "Supports healthy ovulation and cycle regularity.*"
          }
        },
        "p3": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "lead": "Mood.",
            "text": "Supports neurotransmitter signalling linked to mood and emotional balance.*"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "p1",
        "p2",
        "p3"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "[ HOW IT WORKS ]",
        "heading": "How inositol works",
        "text": "<p>Insulin's job is to move sugar out of your blood and into your cells for energy. When cells stop listening, your body makes more of it. High insulin pushes the ovaries toward androgen production, disrupts ovulation and drives the cravings and crashes you feel.</p><p>Inositol is a compound your body already makes and uses. Taken at the studied dose, it supports the signal that tells your cells to take glucose in.*</p>",
        "cta_label": "",
        "cta_link": "",
        "footnote": "<p>*These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. †Supports healthy blood sugar levels already in the normal range.</p>",
        "video": "shopify://files/videos/Video 2_V2_Small.mov",
        "autoplay": true,
        "video_label": "Bodology inositol being stirred into a drink",
        "media_side": "right",
        "media_width": 48,
        "media_ratio": "4 / 3",
        "media_ratio_desktop": "4 / 5",
        "media_radius": 18,
        "page_width": 1240,
        "h_size": 42,
        "h_size_mobile": 30,
        "bg": "#f3eeea",
        "bg_image_opacity": 30,
        "heading_color": "#1a2874",
        "text_color": "#1a2874",
        "accent": "#1b3def",
        "tick_bg": "#1b3def",
        "tick_color": "#ffffff",
